From 82738e0c3c8c5e595c4de9ae28c418ca9a473ef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:17:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Guardian G15b: broad Exodus patterns no longer name a
 tracker

Rows whose network regex is only "any subdomain of one domain"
(every | alternative of the form \.<label>\.<tld>, no groups) are
marked broad; byDomain skips them, byClassName (G17) is unaffected.
With the bundled data: 14 rows. 8 are the intended Google Ads
(\.google\.com) and Facebook (\.facebook\.com) rows, so mail.google.com
or graph.facebook.com no longer show "Google Ads" / "Facebook Audience".
6 are trackers' own domains (ChartBoost, Dynatrace, DOV-E, Glympse,
Lenddo, Cifrasoft) that lose a correct label; nothing is mislabelled.
Reported to the planner as a possible follow-up (an explicit list of
first-party domains instead of the syntactic rule).

withNetwork still counts every row with a regex; broadCount is new.
TrackerDbTest 12 -> 15 groups. Mutations (not skipping broad rows,
treating everything as broad, any-instead-of-all) each fail a test.
All 13 core test classes and policy_check pass. README row added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dphx7H7WfpCsybM6HswWFN
